25
00:01:09,123 --> 00:01:12,259
an Iron Condor, I just want to mention the basics of what it is.

26
00:01:12,260 --> 00:01:14,910
It's just a combination of two vertical spreads.

27
00:01:14,910 --> 00:01:16,729
So you're shorting a call strike,

28
00:01:16,729 --> 00:01:18,548
and then you're buying a call

29
00:01:18,548 --> 00:01:21,579
further out as a protection from the one you're shorting.

30
00:01:21,580 --> 00:01:23,920
And then you're also shorting a put option,

31
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:27,850
and then you're buying another put option further out as protection on this one.

32
00:01:27,850 --> 00:01:32,970
And then the combination of these two vertical spreads right here. So this would be considered a call credit spread.

33
00:01:32,970 --> 00:01:34,430
And this is a put credit spread.

34
00:01:34,430 --> 00:01:39,670
When you combine the both of them together, you get an Iron Condor, sometimes abbreviated as just an IC.

35
00:01:39,670 --> 00:01:43,210
And you're profiting on time decay by being long theta.

36
00:01:43,210 --> 00:01:48,550
So that means as long as the price stays between your strike prices that you've shorted, you'd profit.

37
00:01:48,550 --> 00:01:51,240
You don't need to hold the strategy until expiration.

38
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:56,215
You just need it to stay within your zones for a certain amount of time. And that's how you profit.

39
00:01:56,215 --> 00:01:58,993
And what you're essentially doing is selling these options and

40
00:01:58,993 --> 00:02:01,771
